<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-04-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Busteni	    unloading   rapeseed meal   5,250     India</p>
<p>Matheos	    unloading   corn	     22,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  16,906</p>
<p>				     barley	   15,152</p>
<p>Evangolos	  unloading   sorghum	  35,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Tolga Tomba	unloading   rapeseed meal   3,750     India</p>
<p>Volgobalt 146    arrived     rapeseed	  2,992     Europe</p>
<p>Intrepid	   24/4	  wheat	    15,000     Argentina</p>
<p>Geroi Arsenala    n/a	  sunflower meal  2,200     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobalt 133    25/4	  feed wheat	2,800     Europe</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	27/4	  wheat	    19,120     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   9,386</p>
<p>				     soya	     32,465</p>
<p>Liberty Spirit   28/4	  wheat	    38,300     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  23,034</p>
<p>Amour		29/4	  maize grits     2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Auk		  10/5	  sunflower meal 53,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     + corn + wheat</p>
<p>Europa	     24/5	  corn+barley+   50,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sunflower meal</p>
</text>
